Q: System.CommandLine , exceptions are never caught A: <p>You catch no exceptions because the System.CommandLine like to think of it as a framework, not a library.</p>
<p>You can defeat this behaviour in v2 with</p>
<pre><code>cmd.InvocationConfiguration.EnableDefaultExceptionHandler = false;
// 👆 before 👇
cmd.Invoke();
</code></pre>

Q: Adding input filename to output filename A: <p>Use a substitution to remove the ".txt" from the input filename.
Use string concatenation to build your output file names:</p>

<pre><code>my $infile = 'infile1.txt';

my $prefix = $infile;
$prefix =~ s/\.txt//;  # remove the '.txt', notice the '\' before the dot

# concatenate the prefix and the output filenames
my $outfile1 = $prefix."_outfile1.txt";
my $outfile2 = $prefix."_outfile2.txt";
</code></pre>
